ntake into the store, and read the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:338:   answers becomes the reported one, covering `:published` transactions;\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:339:   in durable mode the HEAD pointer moves — `after-publish` — only after\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:340:   that read-back, so a HEAD never names a manifest the store cannot\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:341:   answer, and a HEAD that cannot be written leaves the round reported\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:345:    (let [{:keys [transactor pool]} (:publication ix)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:346:          {:keys [manifest-address]} (transactor/publish! transactor\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:356:                   :published (:transactions ix)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:363:(defn- consume\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:378:(defn step\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:381:   when any was committed, then drop the publication — its transactor,\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:390:        committed? (> (:transactions ix) (:transactions indexer))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:400:(defn commit-names\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:402:   p}` -- as ONE transaction, then publish the covered indexes at once,\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:403:   the HEAD write included (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md 6.1): one\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:407:   transaction refused is recorded as the failure, like a packet's.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:423:        answer (transactor/transact! (get-in ix [:publication :transactor])\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:428:                           (update :transactions inc)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:433:                               :stage :transact\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:438:(defn skip\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:446:(defn status\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:451:  {:transactions (:transactions indexer)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:453:                    (= (:published indexer) (:transactions indexer)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:459:(defn notice\nsrc