oint, agent-side (docs/design/dao.jing.md,\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:569:      any publication append. Atomic transaction records are flattened here.\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:696:  {[:unresolved :e :tempid] :allocate,\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:699:   [:unresolved :ref-v :tempid] :allocate,\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:702:   [:unresolved :m :tempid] :allocate,\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:705:   [:resolved :e :tempid] :defect,\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:708:   [:resolved :ref-v :tempid] :defect,\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:711:   [:resolved :m :tempid] :defect,\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:716:(defn- id-class\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:722:    (cond (neg? id) :tempid\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:727:(defn- ref-attrs\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:730:   happens only for declared attributes, exactly as the transactor relocates\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:737:(defn- validate-mode!\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:745:(defn- validate-schema!\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:754:(defn- validate-ids!\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:775:(defn session\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:819:                                 ;; recording handle. :test is the seam that\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:845:(defn- tx-record?\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:847:   :dao.space/transaction. The record's own checks (one shared t, non-empty,\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:848:   exactly {:t :datoms}) are admission's, below.\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:850:  (and (map? x) (contains? x :dao.space/transaction)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:853:(defn- d5-shape?\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:866:(defn- normalize-outer\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:871:   nesting; anything else (a scalar, a map that is not a transaction record,\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:887:(defn- admitting-datom?\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:906:(defn- admitting-element\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:908:   rule: a bare row is admitted by the per-datom rule alone; a transaction\ns