or nil (a node over no\n2314:<code>(yin.vm.linker.dht/snapshots node)</code>\n2317:The snapshot vector of 7.2: HEAD and every <code>:loaded</code> index, sorted.\n2327:principal at <code>:seq-floor</code> 0.\n2552:<code>:seq-floor</code>\n2577:HEAD and loaded index manifests\n2588:Linear in the snapshots' datoms\n2593:<code>&lt;dir&gt;/HEAD</code> from disk and rebuild the HEAD index's datoms on\n2596:kept; one is admissible only if invalidated on every HEAD change and every index\n2621:- Tampering with the envelope's name, manifest, sequence, operation or\n2673:  that refuses the manifest blob reports `:unacknowledged`. HEAD has moved\n2767:- Each of `/exhausted`, `/deadline`, `/solo` and `/busy` reaches the\n2796:- `dependency-bindings` over two principals and two snapshots, P1\n2798:  **matching** (both snapshots loaded, both declared) is `:ok` and `app`\n2799:  links and runs; **missing** is `:absent` both when P1's snapshot is not\n2802:  P1 has republished `base` at another address in a loaded snapshot, and\n2857:`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc` (`snapshots`, `names`), the tests beside\n2865:  peer, the round is indexed, HEAD moves, and the publication is `:partial`\n2891:  assertion; a reader of the new snapshot resolves the new address; a\n2892:  reader holding only the old snapshot resolves the old one.\n2893:- The fold over the snapshot set: an undeclared principal and a bad\n2897:  assertion; an envelope present in two snapshots counts once.\n2898:- Only HEAD and loaded index manifests are folded: an envelope blob that is\n2902:- The next sequence is derived from the index after a restart.\n2981:a loaded snapshot, a successful link, and a DHT acknowledgement establish\n3020:FFI or link response uses the emitter's pair; a subsequent new operation\n3039:store and module snapshots, and private resource graph. It also carries\n3187:offer evidence is idempotent by occurrence and snapshot address.\n3190:active lease and attributed holder, offered snapshot vari