{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc | sed -n '334,438p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc | sed -n '1,150p'; rg -n 'load-index|forget|:loads|loaded' src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   334\t(defn- publish\n   335\t  \"Publish the covered indexes over every committed transaction through\n   336\t   the round's transactor, drain its intake into the store, and read the\n   337\t   manifest back from it.  Only a publication whose manifest the store\n   338\t   answers becomes the reported one, covering `:published` transactions;\n   339\t   in durable mode the HEAD pointer moves — `after-publish` — only after\n   340\t   that read-back, so a HEAD never names a manifest the store cannot\n   341\t   answer, and a HEAD that cannot be written leaves the round reported\n   342\t   unpublished.\"\n   343\t  [ix round]\n   344\t  (try\n   345\t    (let [{:keys [transactor pool]} (:publication ix)\n   346\t          {:keys [manifest-address]} (transactor/publish! transactor\n   347\t                                                          (:publish-opts ix))\n   348\t          [n defect] (materialize (:content-store ix) pool)]\n   349\t      (if defect\n   350\t        (assoc ix :failure {:round round :stage :materialize :outcome defect})\n   351\t        (do (index/read-manifest (:content-store ix) manifest-address)\n   352\t            (when-some [write-head! (:after-publish ix)]\n   353\t              (write-head! manifest-address))\n   354\t            (assoc ix\n   355\t                   :manifest-address manifest-address\n   356\t                   :published (:transactions ix)\n   357\t                   :published-payloads n))))\n   358\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   359\t      (assoc ix\n   360\t             :failure {:round round :stage :publish :message (ex-message e)}))))\n   361\t\n   362\t\n   363\t(defn- consume\n   364\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium, handing each\n   365\t   to `f` with the indexer; a gap marks the indexer lost, after which no\n   366\t   packet reaches `f`.\"\n   367\t  [indexer f]\n   368\t  (loop [ix indexer]\n   369\t    (let [{:keys [status batch] observer' :observer}\n   370\t          (observer/observe-next (:observer ix))\n   371\t          ix (assoc ix :observer observer')]\n   372\t      (case status\n   373\t        :ok (recur (if (:lost? ix) ix (f ix batch)))\n   374\t        :gap (recur (assoc ix :lost? true))\n   375\t        ix))))\n   376\t\n   377\t\n   378\t(defn step\n   379\t  \"The round's index step: observe every packet `program-out` still holds\n   380\t   for this observer, commit each through the round's publication, publish\n   381\t   when any was committed, then drop the publication — its transactor,\n   382\t   intake, and pool — so the indexer carries none of this round's payloads\n   383\t   into the next.  A gap is recovered across, counted on the observer's\n   384\t   `:ingress-gaps`, and marks the indexer lost: the missing packet and\n   385\t   every later one are never called indexed.\"\n   386\t  [indexer round]\n   387\t  (let [ix (consume indexer\n   388\t                    (fn [ix packet]\n   389\t                      (first (commit (open-publication ix) packet round))))\n   390\t        committed? (> (:transactions ix) (:transactions indexer))\n   391\t        ;; this round's rows and any an earlier round could not write,\n   392\t        ;; before any publication: no announcement names a missing row\n   393\t        ix (if committed? (write-rows ix round) ix)]\n   394\t    (dissoc (if (and committed? (empty? (:unwritten ix)))\n   395\t              (publish ix round)\n   396\t              ix)\n   397\t            :publication)))\n   398\t\n   399\t\n   400\t(defn commit-names\n   401\t  \"Commit the signed name envelopes `signed` -- each `{:envelope e :proof\n   402\t   p}` -- as ONE transaction, then publish the covered indexes at once,\n   403\t   the HEAD write included (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md 6.1): one\n   404\t   entity per envelope carrying `:yin.module/envelope` and\n   405\t   `:yin.module/proof`, with the session's metadata entity -- `:db/op`,\n   406\t   the session token and `round`, no program root -- in `m`.  A\n   407\t   transaction refused is recorded as the failure, like a packet's.\"\n   408\t  [indexer signed round]\n   409\t  (let [ix (open-publication indexer)\n   410\t        meta-e (:next-e ix)\n   411\t        untimed (fn [e a v m] [e a v nil m])\n   412\t        tx-data (into [(untimed meta-e :db/op :db/assert datom/default-op)\n   413\t                       (untimed meta-e :yin.repl/session (:session-token ix)\n   414\t                                datom/default-op)\n   415\t                       (untimed meta-e :yin.repl/round round datom/default-op)]\n   416\t                      (comp (map-indexed\n   417\t                              (fn [i {:keys [envelope proof]}]\n   418\t                                (let [e (+ meta-e 1 i)]\n   419\t                                  [(untimed e :yin.module/envelope envelope meta-e)\n   420\t                                   (untimed e :yin.module/proof proof meta-e)])))\n   421\t                            cat)\n   422\t                      signed)\n   423\t        answer (transactor/transact! (get-in ix [:publication :transactor])\n   424\t                                     tx-data)]\n   425\t    (dissoc (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n   426\t              (let [ix (-> ix\n   427\t                           (assoc :next-e (+ meta-e 1 (count signed)))\n   428\t                           (update :transactions inc)\n   429\t                           (write-rows round))]\n   430\t                (cond-> ix (empty? (:unwritten ix)) (publish round)))\n   431\t              (assoc ix\n   432\t                     :failure {:round round\n   433\t                               :stage :transact\n   434\t                               :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome answer)}))\n   435\t            :publication)))\n   436\t\n   437\t\n   438\t(defn skip\n     1\t(ns dao.space.transactor\n     2\t  \"The agent-side transactor: a plain value with explicit named operations\n     3\t   over an explicit local dao.stream handle plus an explicit intake pool\n     4\t   of dao.stream writers (docs/design/dao.jing.md, Publication from an\n     5\t   agent; docs/design/dao.space.transactor.md).\n     6\t\n     7\t   A transactor is not a stream in v2 — it is an interpreter over one\n     8\t   (dao.stream.md, Composition): append!/transact! allocate transaction time\n     9\t   and write transaction records through the local stream's writer surface,\n    10\t   and reads go through the caller's own local handle, which the transactor\n    11\t   never owns.\n    12\t\n    13\t   Spec (create!):\n    14\t\n    15\t     {:local-stream s   ; must satisfy stream/reader? and stream/writer?;\n    16\t                        ; supplied, never created, registered, or closed\n    17\t      :intake-pool [p]  ; non-empty; every member satisfies stream/writer?;\n    18\t                        ; supplied, never created, registered, or closed\n    19\t      :name n}          ; optional, diagnostic only\n    20\t\n    21\t   create! validates surfaces, never retention: stream/reader? and\n    22\t   stream/writer? do not establish the complete retention the history scan\n    23\t   requires. The host composition supplies a handle created by\n    24\t   dao.stream.memory-log/create!; supplying an evicting transport is a\n    25\t   host-assembly defect (detectable, deliberately not checked — T18,\n    26\t   docs/design/dao.space.transactor.md).\n    27\t\n    28\t   The transactor owns transaction time. Every append! or transact! writes\n    29\t   exactly ONE atomic transaction record to the local stream\n    30\t\n    31\t     {:dao.space/transaction {:t <nonnegative-integer> :datoms [...]}}\n    32\t\n    33\t   through exactly one local append, so no reader can ever observe a torn\n    34\t   transaction. t is allocated from a per-value watermark: on create! the\n    35\t   retained history is read from its origin (index/snapshot-datoms) and the\n    36\t   next t is derived as 0 for an empty history or 1 + the maximum integer\n    37\t   datom t otherwise. A malformed history throws. The scan is the causality\n    38\t   boundary; a caller-supplied next-t is never accepted.\n    39\t\n    40\t   Operational outcomes are data; argument defects keep throwing. The\n    41\t   watermark advances if and only if the local append answered\n    42\t   :dao.stream/ok, so retrying the identical call re-attempts the identical\n    43\t   t. publish! builds the covered indexes over the local stream and\n    44\t   enqueues them into the intake pool (dao.space.index/publish-index!).\n    45\t   Publication is explicit and acknowledges enqueuing only, never observer\n    46\t   materialization.\n    47\t\n    48\t   Closing is per value: it rejects further appends/transacts with\n    49\t   {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed} but neither closes nor erases\n    50\t   the local stream or the intake pool.\"\n    51\t  (:require [dao.datom :as datom]\n    52\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n    53\t            [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\t(defn- entity->datoms\n    57\t  \"One datom per k/v pair, all sharing transaction time `t`. `:db/id` is\n    58\t   required: a durable log cannot mint per-batch tempids without colliding\n    59\t   across appends. Attribute order within one entity's own datoms is\n    60\t   whatever the host's map iteration yields — unspecified across platforms.\"\n    61\t  [m t]\n    62\t  (when-not (contains? m :db/id)\n    63\t    (throw (ex-info \"entity map requires :db/id\" {:entity m})))\n    64\t  (let [e (:db/id m)]\n    65\t    (mapv (fn [[a v]]\n    66\t            (let [d [e a v t datom/default-op]]\n    67\t              (when-not (datom/local-datom? d)\n    68\t                (throw (ex-info \"invalid persistent local datom\"\n    69\t                                {:datom d, :entity m})))\n    70\t              d))\n    71\t          (remove (fn [[a _v]] (= a :db/id)) m))))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t(defn- pad-datom\n    75\t  \"Pad [e a v] / [e a v t m] to the canonical 5-tuple. The transactor owns\n    76\t   transaction time: a non-nil explicit t is rejected, a nil t is stamped\n    77\t   with the allocated `t`. A nil m takes the default assertion op; an\n    78\t   explicit m (0, a retraction) is preserved.\"\n    79\t  [d t]\n    80\t  (let [[e a v dt dm] d]\n    81\t    (when-not (nil? dt)\n    82\t      (throw\n    83\t        (ex-info\n    84\t          \"the transactor owns transaction time: explicit datom t is rejected\"\n    85\t          {:datom d})))\n    86\t    (let [padded [e a v t (if (nil? dm) datom/default-op dm)]]\n    87\t      (when-not (datom/local-datom? padded)\n    88\t        (throw (ex-info \"invalid persistent local datom\"\n    89\t                        {:datom padded, :input d})))\n    90\t      padded)))\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t(defn- val->datoms\n    94\t  [val t]\n    95\t  (cond\n    96\t    (map? val) (entity->datoms val t)\n    97\t    (and (vector? val) (<= 3 (count val) 5)) [(pad-datom val t)]\n    98\t    :else\n    99\t    (throw\n   100\t      (ex-info\n   101\t        \"a value must be an entity map or datom vector [e a v] / [e a v nil m]\"\n   102\t        {:val val}))))\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\t#_{:clj-kondo/ignore [:unused-binding]}\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(defn- with-write-lock\n   109\t  \"Serialize timestamp allocation and append on hosts with shared-memory\n   110\t   threads. ClojureScript and ClojureDart calls are synchronous within one\n   111\t   isolate, so the direct call has the same single-writer semantics.\"\n   112\t  [lock f]\n   113\t  #?(:clj (locking lock (f))\n   114\t     :default (f)))\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t(defn- derive-next-t\n   118\t  \"Derive the next transaction time from a flattened retained history: 0 for\n   119\t   an empty history, else 1 + the maximum datom t. A datom t that is not a\n   120\t   non-negative integer is a malformed history and throws — this scan is the\n   121\t   causality boundary of the value.\"\n   122\t  [datoms]\n   123\t  (if (empty? datoms)\n   124\t    0\n   125\t    (let [ts (mapv index/datom-t datoms)]\n   126\t      (when-not (every? #(and (integer? %) (<= 0 %)) ts)\n   127\t        (throw\n   128\t          (ex-info\n   129\t            \"malformed retained history: datom t must be a non-negative integer\"\n   130\t            {:history datoms})))\n   131\t      (inc (reduce max ts)))))\n   132\t\n   133\t\n   134\t(defn- append-packet!\n   135\t  \"Append one atomic transaction record to the local stream. The answer is\n   136\t   validated with the contract's own validator before it is interpreted:\n   137\t   :dao.stream/ok advances the watermark and returns the v2 receipt; any\n   138\t   other conforming outcome is returned as data with the watermark\n   139\t   unchanged, so the same t is still pending and retrying the identical\n   140\t   call re-attempts it; a non-outcome answer is folded to\n   141\t   :dao.stream/transport-error with the raw answer retained under\n   142\t   :dao.stream/answer.\"\n   143\t  [local-stream next-t t datoms]\n   144\t  (let [record {:dao.space/transaction {:t t, :datoms datoms}}\n   145\t        answer (stream/append! local-stream record)]\n   146\t    (if-not (stream/valid-outcome? :append! answer)\n   147\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   148\t       :dao.stream/answer answer}\n   149\t      (do (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n   150\t            (swap! next-t inc))\n4:   by any walk, and query a loaded covered index with `dao.space.query/q`\n36:     `load-index` is `load` with the covered-index walk.  Failure\n38:   * `db` and `q` read a loaded index through `dao.space.index/\n45:   `:loaded`, and `:load-failed`.\n309:     :loads {}\n845:  (set (keep #(get-in % [:fetching :address]) (vals (:loads node)))))\n1157:   fetches each missing address and walks again, and reports `:loaded`\n1158:   or `:load-failed` once.  A load already started, loaded or failed is\n1166:  (if (contains? (:loads node) address)\n1168:    (assoc-in node [:loads address]\n1178:(defn load-index\n1180:   covered-index walk: its `:loaded` value is the index's EAVT datoms.\"\n1183:    (throw (ex-info \"dao.space.dht/load-index takes a manifest address\"\n1192:   `{:status :loaded :kind k :fetched n :value v}` or\n1196:             (get-in node [:loads address])]\n1200:      :loaded {:status status :kind kind :fetched fetched :value value}\n1204:(defn forget\n1208:  (when (= :loading (get-in node [:loads address :status]))\n1211:  (update node :loads dissoc address))\n1214:(defn loaded-datoms\n1215:  \"The EAVT datoms of a loaded index, or nil.\"\n1217:  (let [record (get-in node [:loads manifest-address])]\n1218:    (when (and (= :loaded (:status record)) (= index-kind (:kind record)))\n1222:(defn loaded-indexes\n1223:  \"The covered-index manifests whose load is `:loaded` on `node`, as a\n1227:  (vec (sort-by str (filter #(loaded-datoms node %) (keys (:loads node))))))\n1254:  (let [{:keys [kind]} (get-in node [:loads m])]\n1255:    [(update-in node [:loads m] #(-> % (assoc :status :failed :reason reason\n1263:  (let [{:keys [fetching kind walk], :as record} (get-in node [:loads m])\n1277:            node (update-in node [:loads m] assoc :fetching nil :fetched\n1282:          [(update-in node [:loads m] #(-> % (assoc :status :loaded :value\n1285:           [(cond-> {::event :loaded :manifest m :kind kind :fetched fetched}\n1300:                   (assoc-in [:loads m :fetching] {:id id :address a}))\n1316:                                   (:loads node)))]\n1354:          [node loaded] (advance-loads node)\n1356:      [node (-> bound (into unknown) (into lost) (into loaded) (into\n1424:             (some #(= :loading (:status %)) (vals (:loads node)))\n1436:  \"The `dao.space.query` value over the loaded index `manifest-address`\n1437:   names, read from the node's local store.  Throws unless it is loaded.\"\n1439:  (when-not (loaded-datoms node manifest-address)\n1440:    (throw (ex-info (str \"the index \" manifest-address \" is not loaded\")\n1448:  \"`dao.space.query/q` of `query` over the current view of the loaded\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc | sed -n '1,170p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc | sed -n '90,250p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md | sed -n '483,548p'; env | rg -i 'thread|session'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc | sed -n '1,170p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc | sed -n '90,250p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md | sed -n '483,548p'; env | rg -i 'thread|session'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.linker.dht\n     2\t  \"The linker over `dao.jing.dht`, as plain Clojure (docs/design/\n     3\t   yin.vm.linker.dht.md sections 4, 5.4, 7 and 10; slice L2): publish a\n     4\t   module through a `dao.space.dht` node, load its closure onto another\n     5\t   node by manifest address, check its dependency names against the\n     6\t   reader's own name environment, and link it over the node's local store.\n     7\t\n     8\t   The load is `dao.space.dht/load` with the closure walker of\n     9\t   `yin.vm.linker.closure` as its walk: the node stays the only step\n    10\t   owner and fetches each blob the walk answers missing.  A link runs\n    11\t   only after the whole closure is `:loaded`, over a local runtime on the\n    12\t   node's own store, so it asks no peer for anything.\n    13\t\n    14\t   Names come from the reader's composition: the principals it declares\n    15\t   and the index snapshots it chose to load.  Nothing here is read from an\n    16\t   index as authority, and nothing depends on `yin.repl`.\"\n    17\t  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    18\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    19\t            [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n    20\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n    21\t            [dao.space.store :as durable]\n    22\t            [dao.space.store.fs :as fs]\n    23\t            [yin.vm.linker :as linker]\n    24\t            [yin.vm.linker.authority :as authority]\n    25\t            [yin.vm.linker.closure :as closure]\n    26\t            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    27\t            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t(def module-kind\n    31\t  \"The `:kind` of a module closure load.\"\n    32\t  :yin.module/manifest)\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t(defn- refused\n    36\t  [reason data]\n    37\t  (merge {:status :refused :reason reason} data))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t;; =============================================================================\n    41\t;; Publication (5.4)\n    42\t;; =============================================================================\n    43\t\n    44\t(defn publish!\n    45\t  \"`publish-module!` on the node's store: the blobs join the node's\n    46\t   current publication window, reported by the announcement that closes\n    47\t   it.\"\n    48\t  [node spec]\n    49\t  (publish/publish-module! (dht/store node) spec))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(defn publish-name!\n    53\t  \"Publish the module `name` exporting `exports`, derived from the\n    54\t   publisher's own index `db` (`module-from-index`, section 5.3), through\n    55\t   the node's store, and sign what binds the name to it (6.6): answers\n    56\t   `{:status :ok :address a :links {...} :envelopes [...]}`, each envelope\n    57\t   `publish/assertion`'s answer, for the caller to enter into its index\n    58\t   as one transaction (6.1) before it announces.  Without `key` it is\n    59\t   refused `:yin.link.publish/no-key`; any refusal writes nothing.\n    60\t   `opts` also carries `module-from-index`'s `:primitives`, `:modules`\n    61\t   and `:host-modules`.\"\n    62\t  [node db {:keys [key name] :as opts}]\n    63\t  (if-not key\n    64\t    (refused :yin.link.publish/no-key {:name name})\n    65\t    (let [spec (publish/module-from-index db opts)\n    66\t          res (if (= :refused (:status spec)) spec (publish! node spec))]\n    67\t      (if (= :refused (:status res))\n    68\t        res\n    69\t        (assoc (select-keys res [:address :links])\n    70\t               :status :ok\n    71\t               :envelopes (publish/name-envelopes db key name (:address res)))))))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t;; =============================================================================\n    75\t;; The module load (4.3)\n    76\t;; =============================================================================\n    77\t\n    78\t(defn closure-walk\n    79\t  \"The closure walk of `manifest-address` as a `dao.space.dht` load walk:\n    80\t   the walker's three outcomes in the load's three shapes.\"\n    81\t  [manifest-address]\n    82\t  (fn [handle]\n    83\t    (let [w (closure/walk handle manifest-address)]\n    84\t      (case (:yin.link.closure/outcome w)\n    85\t        :missing {::dht/walk :missing :address (:address w)}\n    86\t        :complete {::dht/walk :complete :value w}\n    87\t        :invalid {::dht/walk :invalid :address (:address w) :defect (:defect w)}))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn load-module\n    91\t  \"Start loading the closure of `manifest-address` onto `node`; answers\n    92\t   the node.  `dao.space.dht/step` fetches what is missing.\"\n    93\t  [node manifest-address]\n    94\t  (dht/load node manifest-address {:kind module-kind\n    95\t                                   :walk (closure-walk manifest-address)}))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t(defn module-status\n    99\t  \"The load status of `manifest-address` (4.3), or nil.\"\n   100\t  [node manifest-address]\n   101\t  (dht/load-status node manifest-address))\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t(defn load-refusal\n   105\t  \"The section 9 response row of a failed closure load: `status` as\n   106\t   `module-status` answers it.  `:miss` is `:absent` with the miss\n   107\t   `:cause`, `:invalid` is `:descriptor-defect` with the defect's `:code`\n   108\t   (and its `:detail` and `:text` when present), and `:unaskable` is\n   109\t   `:yin.link.dht/unaskable` with the client's `:outcome`.  nil for a load\n   110\t   that has not failed.  The DHT link source refuses with it.\"\n   111\t  [status]\n   112\t  (when (= :failed (:status status))\n   113\t    (let [{::dht/keys [failure] :keys [address cause defect outcome]} (:reason status)]\n   114\t      (case failure\n   115\t        :miss (refused :absent {:address address :cause cause})\n   116\t        :invalid (refused :descriptor-defect\n   117\t                          (merge {:address address :code (:code defect)}\n   118\t                                 (select-keys defect [:detail :text])))\n   119\t        :unaskable (refused :yin.link.dht/unaskable\n   120\t                            {:address address :outcome outcome})))))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- not-loaded\n   124\t  [node manifest-address]\n   125\t  (refused :yin.link.dht/not-loaded\n   126\t           {:address manifest-address\n   127\t            :load (dissoc (module-status node manifest-address) :value)}))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn- loaded-closure\n   131\t  [node manifest-address]\n   132\t  (let [status (module-status node manifest-address)]\n   133\t    (when (and (= :loaded (:status status)) (= module-kind (:kind status)))\n   134\t      (:value status))))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t;; =============================================================================\n   138\t;; Names: the snapshot set and the fold (7.2, 7.3)\n   139\t;; =============================================================================\n   140\t\n   141\t(defn head\n   142\t  \"The manifest the HEAD of the node's directory names, or nil: a node\n   143\t   over a durable directory store (`dao.space.store`) has one once its\n   144\t   publisher has written it; any other node has none.\"\n   145\t  [node]\n   146\t  (when-some [dir (:durable-dir (dht/local node))]\n   147\t    (some-> (fs/read-file-text dir durable/head-name)\n   148\t            str/trim\n   149\t            edn/read-string\n   150\t            :manifest)))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn snapshots\n   154\t  \"The node's snapshot set (7.2) as the sorted vector of its addresses:\n   155\t   the manifest its directory's HEAD names, when there is one, and every\n   156\t   index manifest whose load is `:loaded`.  Nothing else in the local\n   157\t   store is considered.\"\n   158\t  [node]\n   159\t  (vec (sort-by str (distinct (cond-> (vec (dht/loaded-indexes node))\n   160\t                                (head node) (conj (head node)))))))\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn- snapshot-datoms\n   164\t  \"The datoms of the snapshot `s`: a loaded index's, or HEAD's read from\n   165\t   the node's own store.\"\n   166\t  [node s]\n   167\t  (or (dht/loaded-datoms node s)\n   168\t      (index/read-datoms (dht/local node) s)))\n   169\t\n   170\t\n    90\t                   :dao.stream/cursor\n    91\t                   {:dao.stream.ringbuffer/identity (:identity s)\n    92\t                    ;; The contract's recovery position is the earliest retained\n    93\t                    ;; position, which equals the tail when nothing is retained.\n    94\t                    ;; It must never be an evicted position: a frozen attachment\n    95\t                    ;; whose visible history is fully evicted would otherwise be\n    96\t                    ;; handed its own tail back and re-gap forever.  Recovering\n    97\t                    ;; past that tail is correct; the next read answers `end`.\n    98\t                    :dao.stream.ringbuffer/position (:first s)})\n    99\t            (< pos visible-tail)\n   100\t            ;; `:first`, `:tail`, and `:values` are updated as one state value;\n   101\t            ;; positions in this interval are always retained by the transport.\n   102\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   103\t             :dao.stream/value (get (:values s) pos)\n   104\t             :dao.stream/cursor {:dao.stream.ringbuffer/identity (:identity s)\n   105\t                                 :dao.stream.ringbuffer/position (inc pos)}}\n   106\t            (or (:closed? s) (some? frozen)) (result :dao.stream/end)\n   107\t            :else (result :dao.stream/blocked))))))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t  stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   111\t\n   112\t  (append!\n   113\t    [_ value]\n   114\t    ;; Check attachment liveness *inside* the one state transition.  A deref\n   115\t    ;; before swap! permits an append that began before an attachment close to\n   116\t    ;; land after it; this form gives append!/close! a single linearization point.\n   117\t    (let [out (volatile! nil)]\n   118\t      (swap! state\n   119\t             (fn [s]\n   120\t               (if (or (:closed? s)\n   121\t                       (and (not owner?)\n   122\t                            (not (get-in s [:attachments attachment-id :open?]))))\n   123\t                 (do (vreset! out (result :dao.stream/closed)) s)\n   124\t                 (let [p (:tail s) n (inc p)\n   125\t                       first' (max (:first s) (- n (:capacity s)))]\n   126\t                   (vreset! out (result :dao.stream/ok))\n   127\t                   (-> s (assoc :tail n :first first')\n   128\t                       (assoc :values\n   129\t                              (assoc (if (> first' (:first s))\n   130\t                                       (dissoc (:values s) (:first s))\n   131\t                                       (:values s)) p value)))))))\n   132\t      @out))\n   133\t\n   134\t\n   135\t  stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n   136\t\n   137\t  (close!\n   138\t    [_]\n   139\t    (swap! state\n   140\t           (fn [s]\n   141\t             (if owner?\n   142\t               (assoc s :closed? true)\n   143\t               ;; Preserve the first frozen tail.  Later idempotent closes must\n   144\t               ;; not make post-close values visible through this attachment.\n   145\t               (if (get-in s [:attachments attachment-id :open?])\n   146\t                 (assoc-in s [:attachments attachment-id]\n   147\t                           {:open? false :tail (:tail s)})\n   148\t                 s))))\n   149\t    (result :dao.stream/ok)))\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t(defn create!\n   153\t  \"Create a ring buffer from a creation specification.\"\n   154\t  [spec]\n   155\t  (if-not (valid-spec? spec)\n   156\t    (result :dao.stream/invalid-spec)\n   157\t    (let [state (fresh-state (get spec capacity-key))]\n   158\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   159\t       :dao.stream/handle (RingHandle. state nil true)\n   160\t       :dao.stream/identity (:identity @state)})))\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn- resolve-state\n   164\t  [resolver identity]\n   165\t  (let [x (if (fn? resolver) (resolver identity) (get resolver identity))]\n   166\t    (cond (instance? RingHandle x) (.-state ^RingHandle x)\n   167\t          #?(:cljd false\n   168\t             :clj (instance? clojure.lang.IAtom x)\n   169\t             :cljs (instance? cljs.core/Atom x)) x\n   170\t          :else nil)))\n   171\t\n   172\t\n   173\t(defn attach!\n   174\t  \"Attach using a host-owned resolver (identity -> handle/state).\"\n   175\t  [resolver descriptor]\n   176\t  (if-not (and (map? descriptor)\n   177\t               (= transport-type (:dao.stream/type descriptor))\n   178\t               (contains? descriptor :dao.stream/identity))\n   179\t    (result :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor)\n   180\t    (if-let [state (resolve-state resolver (:dao.stream/identity descriptor))]\n   181\t      ;; A resolver is host composition, not a trusted decoder.  Confirm that\n   182\t      ;; its result actually denotes the descriptor's identity before minting a\n   183\t      ;; handle; otherwise a mis-keyed directory silently attaches elsewhere.\n   184\t      (if (= (:dao.stream/identity descriptor) (:identity @state))\n   185\t        (let [id (str (random-uuid))]\n   186\t          (swap! state assoc-in [:attachments id] {:open? true})\n   187\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   188\t           :dao.stream/handle (RingHandle. state id false)\n   189\t           :dao.stream/attachment id})\n   190\t        (result :dao.stream/not-found))\n   191\t      (result :dao.stream/not-found))))\n   192\t\n   193\t\n   194\t(defn make-attacher\n   195\t  \"Return a unary attach! closure over host-owned resolver state.\n   196\t   This small directory is composition/test infrastructure, never a registry\n   197\t   owned by DaoStream or this namespace.\"\n   198\t  [resolver]\n   199\t  (fn [descriptor] (attach! resolver descriptor)))\n   483\t### 5.8 Command line and saved state (decision 8)\n   484\t\n   485\t- **The token** is `yin:<host:port>/<principal>`. The publisher prints it\n   486\t  once, when its socket binds, not after each publication: it no longer\n   487\t  changes. A three-part token is refused with the message that a manifest\n   488\t  is a pin and belongs to `--dht-manifest`.\n   489\t- **`dht join <token>`** becomes `--index-store dht:<dir> --dht-peer\n   490\t  <host:port> --dht-principal <hex> --dht-follow <hex>`.\n   491\t- **Its first manifest** comes from the first trace it honours, by 5.5.\n   492\t  The shell admits evaluation at once and says, per followed principal,\n   493\t  whether a head is installed. It does not block the prompt on a\n   494\t  publisher: 5.6 parks the require instead.\n   495\t- **`--dht-manifest` with a saved `--dht-follow`**: the pin wins for that\n   496\t  run. The banner says following is suspended and `heads.edn` is neither\n   497\t  read as a snapshot nor written.\n   498\t- **`state.edn`** keeps flags, as now. It gains `--dht-follow`\n   499\t  (repeatable). It never holds a head; `heads.edn` does.\n   500\t  `--dht-manifest` stays one-shot.\n   501\t- **Hydration into HEAD is removed** (D1): `refused-head`, `hydrated`\n   502\t  and the `::hydrating` admission gate go. A pinned index that cannot\n   503\t  load still refuses the shell, as now.\n   504\t- The banner of a publishing node with a key states that its head is\n   505\t  served to any peer that asks its address, and the banner of a following\n   506\t  node names whom it follows and that it re-serves their heads when it\n   507\t  publishes.\n   508\t\n   509\t### 5.9 Failure and security (decision 9)\n   510\t\n   511\tSection 9 is the table. The rules it rests on:\n   512\t\n   513\t- A trace is honoured only when it verifies under a key the reader\n   514\t  declared. Who served it is never evidence.\n   515\t- A head is installed only after its whole index is local and its\n   516\t  sequence is confirmed by that index.\n   517\t- The floor never moves down and survives a restart.\n   518\t- No failure retracts an installed head, and none waits on a clock.\n   519\t\n   520\t### 5.10 Portability (decision 10)\n   521\t\n   522\t**Portable `.cljc`, identical on the JVM, Node and Dart:** the trace, its\n   523\tsigned bytes and the rule of 5.5 (`yin.vm.linker.head`); the board and\n   524\tthe follower's step; the node's mirror and reflections\n   525\t(`dao.stream.remote`, `dao.stream.udp`, both portable today); the\n   526\trendering of `heads.edn`.\n   527\t\n   528\t**Host seams, all existing:** Ed25519 (`yin.vm.linker.sign`); the\n   529\tdatagram bind (`dao.stream.datagram.*`); the atomic file replace\n   530\t(`dao.space.store.fs`). No new seam is needed.\n   531\t\n   532\t**A browser** has no UDP and no Ed25519 primitive here: it follows\n   533\tnothing, as it resolves no signed name (6.4). A WebSocket source is the\n   534\troute when signed names reach a browser build.\n   535\t\n   536\t**ClojureDart traps to design against:**\n   537\t\n   538\t- `heads.edn` is rendered with no whitespace before a closing bracket and\n   539\t  read back by test on Dart; its reader refuses `{:k 1 }`.\n   540\t- Host branches are written `#?(:cljd ... :clj ... :cljs ...)` with\n   541\t  `:cljd` first; `:clj` alone does not exclude the Dart build.\n   542\t- A protocol or reify method never takes `[_ _]`; a second ignored\n   543\t  parameter is named.\n   544\t- No test reaches a private var by `#'ns/name` across namespaces; a\n   545\t  helper a test needs is public.\n   546\t- The sequence is an index `t`. It stays within 2^53 so the same integer\n   547\t  is exact on Node, and the vectors include a sequence above 2^32.\n   548\t- A manifest address decoded from the wire is compared with `=`, never\nCLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION=1\nCLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ATTENDED=0\nCLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=7fdf0e81-ee16-4edd-b52f-d276b49cb586\nCODEX_SESSION_ID=01a10c19-e77f-7631-b9d5-f26df7a7ff2f\nCODEX_THREAD_ID=01a10c19-e77f-7631-b9d5-f26df7a7ff2f\nSECURITYSESSIONID=186af\nTERM_SESSION_ID=AF702B04-01A8-4BE4-8C3E-4C54FCAF4B1F\n__MISE_\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
