{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc | sed -n '370,515p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc | sed -n '620,755p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.md | sed -n '272,288p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.jing.dht.md | sed -n '670,708p'; rg -n 'defn.*replace|HEAD|head-name' src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc; rg -n 'whitespace|interned|private|cljd|2\\\\\"'^53'\"' docs/agents/build-n-test.md | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"   370\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   371\t   :dao.stream.remote/reason e})\n   372\t\n   373\t\n   374\t(defn- learn!\n   375\t  \"The attach probe's ok: record the source's descriptor and declared\n   376\t   surface, plus :closable.\"\n   377\t  [refl answer]\n   378\t  (swap! refl assoc\n   379\t         :source-descriptor (:dao.stream/descriptor answer)\n   380\t         :surface (conj (into #{} (:dao.stream.remote/surface answer))\n   381\t                        :closable)))\n   382\t\n   383\t\n   384\t(defn- install-more!\n   385\t  \"Install each more outcome under the answer's served identity and at\n   386\t   the cursor that precedes it, so a later next at that cursor by a\n   387\t   reflection of the same stream returns the source's own outcome\n   388\t   without a request. The identity is half of the key: two served\n   389\t   identities can carry equal cursor values, and an outcome belongs to\n   390\t   its own stream.\"\n   391\t  [link answer]\n   392\t  (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity answer)]\n   393\t    (loop [cur (:dao.stream/cursor answer)\n   394\t           more (:dao.stream.remote/more answer)]\n   395\t      (when (and cur (seq more))\n   396\t        (let [[o & further] more]\n   397\t          (swap! link assoc-in [:filed-cursors [identity cur]] o)\n   398\t          (recur (:dao.stream/cursor o) further))))))\n   399\t\n   400\t\n   401\t(defn- absorb!\n   402\t  \"Consume one value read off the channel. A well-formed answer whose\n   403\t   id is outstanding and whose identity is the outstanding entry's\n   404\t   reflection's own identity is taken: a not-found error marks the\n   405\t   reflection gone; the attach probe's ok records the source's\n   406\t   descriptor and declared surface; an append!'s source outcome is\n   407\t   emitted on the event writer, correlated by id; any other answer is\n   408\t   filed under its id and its more outcomes installed. Answers whose\n   409\t   id is not outstanding, answers whose identity is not the\n   410\t   reflection's own -- a mismatch never completes a request, which\n   411\t   stays outstanding -- and values that are not well-formed answers,\n   412\t   are dropped as diagnostics.\"\n   413\t  [link v]\n   414\t  (when (well-formed-answer? v)\n   415\t    (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id v)]\n   416\t      (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n   417\t        (let [refl (:reflection entry)\n   418\t              req (:req entry)\n   419\t              op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n   420\t              e (:dao.stream.remote/error v)]\n   421\t          (when (= (:dao.stream/identity v) (:identity @refl))\n   422\t            (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)\n   423\t            (swap! refl update :ids disj id)\n   424\t            (cond\n   425\t              (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found e)\n   426\t              (do (swap! refl assoc :gone? true)\n   427\t                  (when (or (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n   428\t                            (= :dao.stream/append! op))\n   429\t                    (emit! link v)))\n   430\t\n   431\t              (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n   432\t              ;; The attach probe's confirmation. ok records; a\n   433\t              ;; no-surface or oversize error marks nothing.\n   434\t              (when (nil? e)\n   435\t                (learn! refl v)\n   436\t                (emit! link v))\n   437\t\n   438\t              (= :dao.stream/append! op)\n   439\t              (emit! link v)\n   440\t\n   441\t              :else\n   442\t              (do (swap! link assoc-in\n   443\t                         [:filed id] {:req req :ans v :reflection refl})\n   444\t                  (install-more! link v)))))))))\n   445\t\n   446\t\n   447\t(defn- channel-loss!\n   448\t  \"The channel reader answered end: the channel is gone. The link\n   449\t   abandons its outstanding ids, reporting each abandoned append! on\n   450\t   the event writer as append-unknown; filed answers are kept and\n   451\t   still returned; reattachment is the caller's policy.\"\n   452\t  [link]\n   453\t  (doseq [[id entry] (:outstanding @link)]\n   454\t    (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n   455\t      (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\n   456\t                   :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\n   457\t                   :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\n   458\t    (swap! (:reflection entry) update :ids disj id))\n   459\t  (swap! link assoc :outstanding {} :channel-gone? true))\n   460\t\n   461\t\n   462\t(defn- retry-pending!\n   463\t  \"One more try of each probe the writer has refused, once per drain,\n   464\t   until a send is accepted; the accepted send is registered as the\n   465\t   outstanding probe and the normal filing path confirms it.\"\n   466\t  [link]\n   467\t  (doseq [[_ e] (:pending @link)]\n   468\t    (send-request! link (:reflection e) (:req e))))\n   469\t\n   470\t\n   471\t(defn- drain!\n   472\t  \"Read the link's channel reader to blocked, filing each answer: the\n   473\t   caller's own polling is the cadence and no driver step exists. An\n   474\t   end is the channel's loss; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery\n   475\t   cursor, the lost wire values being lost. Each drain is also one\n   476\t   further ask of an outstanding descriptor probe -- the probe's\n   477\t   caller never asks it remotely -- so resend-after re-sends it, and\n   478\t   one more try of each probe the writer has refused, until a send\n   479\t   is accepted.\"\n   480\t  [link]\n   481\t  (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n   482\t    (doseq [[_ e] (:outstanding @link)]\n   483\t      (when (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req e)))\n   484\t        (count-ask! link (:dao.stream.remote/id (:req e)))))\n   485\t    (retry-pending! link)\n   486\t    (loop []\n   487\t      (let [r (stream/next (:reader @link) (:cursor @link))]\n   488\t        (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   489\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   490\t          (do (absorb! link (:dao.stream/value r))\n   491\t              (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   492\t              (recur))\n   493\t          :dao.stream/blocked nil\n   494\t          :dao.stream/end (channel-loss! link)\n   495\t          :dao.stream/gap\n   496\t          (do (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r)) nil)\n   497\t          nil)))))\n   498\t\n   499\t\n   500\t;; =============================================================================\n   501\t;; The reflection (2.4)\n   502\t;; =============================================================================\n   503\t\n   504\t(defn- result\n   505\t  [outcome]\n   506\t  {:dao.stream/outcome outcome})\n   507\t\n   508\t\n   509\t(defn- refl-descriptor\n   510\t  \"Local: ok with the remote descriptor the reflection was attached\n   511\t   with and the identity -- the same identity as the source's own\n   512\t   descriptor, different reachability. A name outlives what it named:\n   513\t   descriptor still answers ok once gone, once closed, and after\n   514\t   channel loss.\"\n   515\t  [refl]\n   620\t\n   621\t      (:gone? @refl) (translated :dao.stream.remote/not-found)\n   622\t\n   623\t      (surface-lacks? refl :dao.stream/next)\n   624\t      (translated :dao.stream.remote/no-surface)\n   625\t\n   626\t      :else\n   627\t      (or (filed-next! link refl c)\n   628\t          (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n   629\t            (send-or-count! link refl :dao.stream/next c)\n   630\t            (result :dao.stream/blocked))\n   631\t          (translated :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone)))))\n   632\t\n   633\t\n   634\t(defn- refl-append\n   635\t  \"The append! operation: send the request and return the channel\n   636\t   writer's outcome -- ok is acceptance on the outbound path, exactly\n   637\t   the contract's Writing rule for a transport that carries values\n   638\t   toward a stream elsewhere. The source's outcome is emitted on the\n   639\t   event writer when it is filed, correlated by id; append! never\n   640\t   answers the source's full. Only an accepted send is in flight: a\n   641\t   refused append! never crossed, so its effect is not unknown.\"\n   642\t  [refl v]\n   643\t  (let [link (:link @refl)]\n   644\t    (drain! link)\n   645\t    (cond\n   646\t      (:closed? @refl) (result :dao.stream/closed)\n   647\t      (:gone? @refl) (translated :dao.stream.remote/not-found)\n   648\t      (surface-lacks? refl :dao.stream/append!)\n   649\t      (translated :dao.stream.remote/no-surface)\n   650\t      :else\n   651\t      (let [req (wire-request link refl :dao.stream/append! [v])\n   652\t            r (stream/append! (:writer @link) req)]\n   653\t        (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   654\t          (register! link refl req))\n   655\t        r))))\n   656\t\n   657\t\n   658\t(defn- refl-close\n   659\t  \"The close! operation, local: the reflection forgets its\n   660\t   outstanding ids and its kept, unsent probe, reporting each\n   661\t   outstanding append! on the event writer as append-unknown -- an\n   662\t   append whose answer never arrives has unknown effect; afterwards\n   663\t   append! answers closed, cursor answers closed, next answers filed\n   664\t   outcomes then end, and nothing crosses the wire. Idempotent, per\n   665\t   the contract's Close.\"\n   666\t  [refl]\n   667\t  (let [link (:link @refl)]\n   668\t    (swap! link update :pending\n   669\t           (fn [kept]\n   670\t             (into {}\n   671\t                   (remove (fn [[_ e]]\n   672\t                             (= refl (:reflection e)))\n   673\t                           kept))))\n   674\t    (drain! link)\n   675\t    (when-not (:closed? @refl)\n   676\t      (doseq [id (:ids @refl)]\n   677\t        (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n   678\t          (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n   679\t            (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\n   680\t                         :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\n   681\t                         :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\n   682\t          (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)))\n   683\t      (swap! refl assoc :closed? true :ids #{}))\n   684\t    (result :dao.stream/ok)))\n   685\t\n   686\t\n   687\t(deftype ReflectionHandle\n   688\t  [state]\n   689\t\n   690\t  stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   691\t\n   692\t  (descriptor\n   693\t    [_]\n   694\t    (refl-descriptor state))\n   695\t\n   696\t\n   697\t  stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   698\t\n   699\t  (cursor\n   700\t    [_ anchor]\n   701\t    (refl-cursor state anchor))\n   702\t\n   703\t\n   704\t  (next\n   705\t    [_ c]\n   706\t    (refl-next state c))\n   707\t\n   708\t\n   709\t  stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   710\t\n   711\t  (append!\n   712\t    [_ v]\n   713\t    (refl-append state v))\n   714\t\n   715\t\n   716\t  stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n   717\t\n   718\t  (close!\n   719\t    [_]\n   720\t    (refl-close state)))\n   721\t\n   722\t\n   723\t;; =============================================================================\n   724\t;; The remote descriptor dispatch (2.2)\n   725\t;; =============================================================================\n   726\t\n   727\t(defn- valid-remote-descriptor?\n   728\t  \"A remote descriptor names a stream and a channel: the generic\n   729\t   envelope rules, the :dao.stream/remote type, and a channel\n   730\t   descriptor. It carries no authorization, no surface and no\n   731\t   anchors; the mirror answers those.\"\n   732\t  [d]\n   733\t  (and (stream/valid-descriptor? d)\n   734\t       (= :dao.stream/remote (:dao.stream/type d))\n   735\t       (contains? d :dao.stream/channel)))\n   736\t\n   737\t\n   738\t(defn attacher\n   739\t  \"The composition's :dao.stream/attach entry for :dao.stream/remote\n   740\t   descriptors; a dynamic dispatch table has this entry and no\n   741\t   :dao.stream/create one, because attaching through this transport\n   742\t   never creates. `opts` carries the composition data:\n   743\t   :dao.stream.remote/channels maps each channel descriptor this peer\n   744\t   reaches to its own end {:reader r :writer w} -- two ring buffers in\n   745\t   one process today, the ws, udp and pair channels of section 3\n   746\t   later; :dao.stream.remote/events is the optional event writer the\n   747\t   links emit on; :dao.stream.remote/resend-after is the links'\n   748\t   resend-after k, unbounded on an ordered reliable channel and small\n   749\t   on udp; :dao.stream.remote/budget is the budget stamped on every\n   750\t   next request. One link is kept per channel descriptor, shared by\n   751\t   every reflection through that channel. attach! answers ok at once\n   752\t   with a reflection handle and a local, opaque\n   753\t   :dao.stream/attachment -- the contract's deferred remote\n   754\t   confirmation -- and the link sends one descriptor probe for the\n   755\t   identity: its answer is the reflection's confirmation, not-found\n   272\treference. It is reachability data, not the logical-stream identity itself.\n   273\tIts properties are settled:\n   274\t\n   275\t- It carries `:dao.stream/type` — the transport, as above — as its dispatch\n   276\t  key.\n   277\t- It carries the logical-stream identity under the contract-owned\n   278\t  `:dao.stream/identity` key. Different descriptors may reach\n   279\t  the same logical stream through different endpoints of the same owning\n   280\t  transport; their reachability data\n   281\t  may differ, but their logical-stream identity is structurally equal. The same\n   282\t  descriptor attaches to the same stream every time. A logical stream is the\n   283\t  sequence one transport instance owns: a copy on another host or medium is a\n   284\t  different logical stream with its own identity, and that it mirrors the\n   285\t  first is a fact for an interpreter to record.\n   286\t- It is self-contained. If the stream is remote, it contains whatever is\n   287\t  needed to connect — perhaps an IP address and port. The entry data is\n   288\t  transport-owned; a handler that cannot make sense of it returns\n   670\t## 8. Hardening\n   671\t\n   672\tImplemented where the DHT reads raw events, never in the raw layer. Non-loopback\n   673\texposure requires the S4 secret and inbound bound in the socket composition.\n   674\t\n   675\t- **Cookie protocol.** Every reply carries a cookie for the requester's\n   676\t  observed address. A requester keeps the newest cookie each peer gave it and\n   677\t  echoes it in every later request and request chunk to that peer. A cookie\n   678\t  is 16 bytes, is a pure function `cookie-for` of the epoch and the observed\n   679\t  host and port, with `epoch = floor(now / cookie-epoch-ticks)`, and is valid\n   680\t  under the current or the previous epoch. Verification recomputes and\n   681\t  compares; it holds no state. The protocol, the gate below and freshness\n   682\t  (4.1) are one mechanism, implemented whole in S2.\n   683\t- **`cookie-for` has two definitions, and only it differs between slices.**\n   684\t  - *S2 stand-in:* the first 16 bytes of `SHA-256(epoch | observed-host |\n   685\t    observed-port)`. Unkeyed and deterministic, so tests can predict it, and\n   686\t    forgeable, which is why exposure stays loopback-only.\n   687\t  - *S4 replacement:* the first 16 bytes of `MAC(epoch-secret, observed-host |\n   688\t    observed-port)` with `epoch-secret = MAC(:dao.jing.dht/secret, epoch)`.\n   689\t    The MAC is HMAC-SHA-256 from each host's library; nothing is\n   690\t    hand-rolled. The root secret is, per node, at least 32 random bytes\n   691\t    from the host CSPRNG, minted at composition, in-memory only, never\n   692\t    persisted or shared. Note that the tests share one secret for\n   693\t    predictability.\n   694\t    From S4 a socket composition without a secret is a composition defect.\n   695\t  The wire, the state and every other rule are identical under both.\n   696\t- **The gate.** A request or request chunk without a valid cookie causes no\n   697\t  work: no lookup, no storage, no reassembly, no routing entry. The only\n   698\t  possible response is the **need-cookie reply**, exactly\n   699\t  `{:dao.jing.dht/v 1 :op :reply :q n :id <32 bytes> :cookie <16 bytes>\n   700\t  :need-cookie true}` and nothing else.\n   701\t- **No amplification, without exception.** The need-cookie reply is sent only\n   702\t  if its encoded length is less than or equal to the length of the datagram\n   703\t  that caused it. Otherwise the datagram is dropped in **silence**. There is\n   704\t  no other reply to an unproven source.\n   705\t- **First contact is padded.** A requester sending without a cookie adds\n   706\t  `:pad`, a zero-filled byte string, so that the datagram is at least\n   707\t  `first-contact-bytes` long. `first-contact-bytes` is 256, a constant of\n   708\t  wire v1. S2 proves by test that the need-cookie reply never encodes to more\n6:   replacement for HEAD. CLJ, Node, and Dart each implement them with\n31:   HEAD replacement writes the whole record to a temp file in the same\n33:   syncs it, and renames it over HEAD — rename is the atomicity, so a\n34:   torn, short, or interrupted write is never observed as HEAD.\n263:  \"True when this host can open a directory and fsync it, so a HEAD\n335:(defn atomic-replace!\n390:   the store's HEAD parsing uses.\"\n14:# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\n17:bb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\n20:bb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n23:bb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n85:clj -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n91:The Dart `bb` lanes run `src/dev/cljd_agg.clj` (`bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\n92:[--slow-only | --slow-regex]`), not `cljd test`. `--slow-only` runs only the\n98:each of the ~166 generated `test/cljd-out/**/*_test.dart` files, so the\n99:script compiles every test namespace via `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n100:<namespaces>`, writes up to min(8, cores) shard files under `build/cljd-agg/`\n103:under `test/`, so plain `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd test` still works. Tests of\n107:`flutter test`/`cljd test` globs everything under `test/cljd-out/`, and the\n110:stale file can silently pass a plain `cljd test`. Run `rm -rf test/cljd-out`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
